right: `4 [[95], [75, 20], [60, 40], [50]]`. The heaviest person left always gets a canoe, shared with the lightest when they fit; the last person, 50 kg, has nobody left to pair with.
wrong: 95 + 20 is over 100: alone. 75 + 20 = 95: they share. 60 + 40 = 100: they share. Then `light` and `heavy` both point at 50: alone.

